<title>INDIA: India soybean, meal steady, oil down.</title>
<headline>India soybean, meal steady, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in very thin trade as arrivals were poor, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 800 tonnes in the markets of central India as compared to around 15,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne on increased supplies from refineries against limited demand. Soyoil solvent was steady. Business volume was dull and the undertone steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in limited trade. Soymeal yellow was $304-305 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $115-116 per tonne FAS in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,000 rupees in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady. Selling from Indian processors and exporters was very limited as availability was poor.</p>
